## **SLIDE 2 — Storage, Data Efficiency & Engineering Best Practices**

### **📦 Storage / Space Optimization (Delta vs Raw JMS Writes)**

| Aspect             | JMS (Before)              | Delta (After)        | Benefit              |
| ------------------ | ------------------------- | -------------------- | -------------------- |
| Write pattern      | Individual message writes | Micro-batched writes | Fewer small files    |
| File format        | Raw / semi-structured     | **Delta (Parquet)**  | Columnar compression |
| Schema enforcement | Weak                      | **Strong**           | Less bad data stored |
| Data corruption    | SOM failures possible     | **Zero corruption**  | No re-ingestion      |

**Estimated storage reduction:**
➡️ **20–30% lower storage footprint** due to:

* Parquet compression
* Schema pruning
* Removal of corrupted replays

> Example:
> 10 TB/year → **2–3 TB saved/year**
> S3 @ ~$23/TB/month → **$550–$800/year saved**

